ilya2@rcn.com wrote:
> Someone else started a thread on how to convert an altar without
> fighting the attendant priest. His solution is to wall the priest off
> with boulders. That post started a lively discussion on the advantages
> of killing the priest vs. not killing him. My two questions:
>
> 1. Can you keep the priest at bay with pits instead of boulders? Will
> he still cast spells on you or, worse, somehow get across the pits?
>
> 2. Do you lose alignment (as some claimed) or gain alignment for
> killing a priest of another faith? I can understand losing LUCK for
> attacking/angering a peaceful human, but shouldn't you GAIN alignment
> for killing someone opposed to your god? Or does that work for chaotics
> only?

Priests will still cast spells if you are within their line of sight.
This means that pits will not stop a priest from casting spells, since
a pit does not block line of sight. However, priests more than 7
squares away from you will not cast spells.

I've never had priests (nor shopkeepers) get past a pit.  However, I've
seen many other monsters that did get past a pit.  Unfortunately, I am
not completely sure if priests can't get past pits.



